# R50 git guardrails (agents)

**Full command recipes:** `.cursor/rules/git-release-workflow.mdc`. This file is the **safety layer** — classify work first, then run only the matching track.

## One question before any git work

**Is this R50 redesign UI work** (mode toggle, player, redesign slices per `_docs/planning/REDESIGN/`)?

| Answer | Track | Integration branch | Production site |
|--------|-------|-------------------|-----------------|
| **Yes** | **Track 2** | `r50-overhaul` | https://stage.bananasutra.com |
| **No** | **Track 1** | `staging` → `main` (with approval) | https://bananasutra.com |
| **Unsure** | **Stop** | Ask Banana | Do not guess |

**Shared code** (`bbb-api/`, `workers/`, generated data, hotfixes): almost always **Track 1**, even during the overhaul — unless Banana explicitly says the change is redesign-only on `r50-overhaul`.

---

## Track 2 — redesign only (keeps `main` clean)

**Use when:** catalog app redesign slices, anything that should preview on staging redesign URL.

| Step | Do |
|------|-----|
| Branch from | `r50-overhaul` (pulled) |
| Work branch | `feat/r50-ui-overhaul-<slice>` |
| Merge into | **`r50-overhaul` only** |
| Verify | https://stage.bananasutra.com |
| End session on | `r50-overhaul` (pulled) |

```bash
git checkout r50-overhaul && git pull origin r50-overhaul
git checkout -b feat/r50-ui-overhaul-<slice>
# … commits on feat branch …
git checkout r50-overhaul && git pull origin r50-overhaul
git merge --no-ff feat/r50-ui-overhaul-<slice> -m "merge feat/r50-ui-overhaul-<slice> (R50 <what shipped>)"
git push origin r50-overhaul
```

### Track 2 — forbidden (agents must refuse)

- Merge `feat/r50-ui-overhaul-*` into **`staging`** or **`main`**
- Merge **`r50-overhaul`** into **`staging`** or **`main`** (except final R50 ship — see below)
- Merge **`staging`** into **`r50-overhaul`** (wrong direction)
- Cherry-pick redesign commits onto Track 1 branches without Banana’s explicit plan
- `git push origin main` or `staging → main` for redesign work

**Final R50 ship to production** (once, end of overhaul): only after Banana explicitly approves → `r50-overhaul` → `staging` → `main` with subject `release: merge staging (R50 redesign overhaul)`. See `git-release-workflow.mdc`.

---

## Track 1 — production lane (unchanged)

**Use when:** data refresh, hotfix, BBB/worker fix, copy on live site, numbered release R51/R52…, anything that must ship to **bananasutra.com** during the overhaul.

| Step | Do |
|------|-----|
| Branch from | `staging` (pulled) |
| Work branch | `feat/r##-<scope>` (not `r50-ui-overhaul`) |
| Merge into | **`staging`** |
| Production | **`staging` → `main` only after explicit Banana approval** |
| End session on | `staging` (pulled) unless Banana asks otherwise |

```bash
git checkout staging && git pull origin staging
git checkout -b feat/r##-<scope>
# … commits …
git checkout staging && git pull origin staging
git merge --no-ff feat/r##-<scope> -m "merge feat/r##-<scope> (<what shipped>)"
git push origin staging
# STOP — ask before staging → main
```

Production merge subject (first line only): `release: merge staging (<one-line what shipped>)`.

---

## Keeping redesign current with production (maintenance, not every PR)

After **`main`** gets data or hotfixes, **`r50-overhaul`** should absorb them so staging doesn’t drift:

```bash
git checkout r50-overhaul && git pull origin r50-overhaul
git merge origin/main
# resolve conflicts if any
git push origin r50-overhaul
```

Run when Banana asks, or after a data release on `main` — not as part of every redesign slice.

---

## Sanity check (run before merge/push)

```bash
git branch --show-current
```

| Current branch | About to merge | OK? |
|----------------|----------------|-----|
| `feat/r50-ui-overhaul-*` | → `r50-overhaul` | Yes |
| `feat/r50-ui-overhaul-*` | → `staging` / `main` | **No** |
| `feat/r##-*` (not r50-ui) | → `staging` | Yes |
| `feat/r##-*` | → `r50-overhaul` | **No** (unless Banana says otherwise) |
| `r50-overhaul` | → `main` | **No** (until final R50 approval) |
| any | `git push --force` on `main` / `staging` / `r50-overhaul` | **No** unless Banana explicitly requests |

